.TH FLATTOPS 1
.SH NAME
flattops \- carrier task-force game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/flattops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I FlatTops
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Games/FlatTops.HC
carrier task force game.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A help panel listing the three mouse actions is shown at startup; the
simulation is held until any key dismisses it.
.PP
Button 1 sets the course of the squadron nearest the point clicked;
button 2 launches a squadron from the nearest carrier toward the
point; a right double-tap on a squadron sends it home.
Ships carry fuel and a damage bitmap: hits burn holes in it and
repairs fill them back in, so a ship is lost when the burning
outruns the repair.
Destroy the enemy force.
.PP
Plus and minus scale
.IR "game speed" ,
which multiplies the rate at which everything \- movement, fuel burn,
repair and the odds of a torpedo hit \- advances per real second.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "RMB double-tap"
.TP
.B "any key"
Dismiss the startup help and begin
.TP
.B LMB
Set friendly squadron heading toward point
.TP
.B RMB
Launch squadron toward point
.TP
.B "RMB double-tap"
Return squadron
.TP
.B + / =
Increase game speed
.TP
.B - / _
Decrease game speed
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/flattops_1.bit
Ship sprites, one
.IB name .bit
and
.IB name .mask
per ship type and player, from the
.B $SP
bins of the original.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/flattops.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original's File and Play pulldown menus are not drawn; their
entries are all on keys.
The window is a fixed 800x600 rather than a scrollable maximized task,
so there is no Ctrl-Left grab scrolling.
Squadron return is a right double-tap within 400ms and 20 pixels,
standing in for the original's
.BR MSG_MS_R_D_UP .
